  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "The Canyons at Dellwood Park is the crown jewel of Chicago-area disc golf — a 27-hole championship layout in a historic park with moderate hills, woods, and eight water hazards in play. Since 2014 it's been the course the region's best players measure themselves against.",
    "The course is a true 27-holer with alternate holes on 6 and 8: the variant holes (6A–6E and 8A–8D) let you build your own loop and keep the course fresh every visit. Trash cans and picnic tables at every hole, and the Dellwood Disc Golf shop is on site.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Mach X baskets, it's a full day of championship golf in a park that's been part of Lockport's landscape for over a century."
  ],
