  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 8 is the longest standard hole at The Canyons at 450 feet — a par 4 where the park's eight water hazards make their most serious appearance. It's the hole that defines the course's championship character: woods, water, and a line that rewards both power and nerve. The 8A–8D variants give you four more ways to lose a disc nearby.",
  "localTips": "Twenty-seven holes with variant holes on 6 (6A–6E) and 8 (8A–8D) — build your own loop and it plays different every visit. The Dellwood Disc Golf shop is on site. Free to play in a historic park; expect a serious full-day round.",
